course: dictionary
lesson: 14379
title: Organism
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An organism is any living thing. Animals, plants, fungi like mushrooms, and bacteria are all organisms. «A dog, an oak tree and a mushroom are all organisms.» Each one is alive, so each one needs to take in food, water or energy to stay alive.
explain: Some organisms are too small to see. We call these micro-organisms. «The drop of pond water was full of micro-organisms that you could only see under a microscope.» The prefix micro means very small, so a micro-organism is a very small living thing.
explain: Scientists also use organism for a whole system with parts that work together, like a living thing. You will see this in your science lessons. Think about the words around it: when the text says «the whole organism», it means all the parts working as one.
fact: An organism is any living thing, such as an animal, plant, fungus or bacterium.
fact: A micro-organism is an organism too small to see without a microscope.
fact: A single-celled organism is made of just one cell.
fact: All organisms need food, water and energy to stay alive.
fact: In a food chain, organisms eat or are eaten.
exercise: «An oak tree is an organism.» What is an organism? | A machine that runs on electricity | A tool used in a science lab | A rock or stone that never changes | *A living thing, such as an animal, plant, fungus or bacterium
exercise: Which of these is an organism? | rock | water | pebble | *mushroom
exercise: «The pond was full of micro-organisms too small to see.» What does micro-organism mean? | *A living thing too small to see without a microscope | A large animal that lives in the water | A plant with big green leaves | A kind of rock found at the bottom of a pond
test: «All organisms need food, water and energy.» What do all organisms need? | *Food, water and energy | Money | Toys and books | Sunshine only
test: In a food chain, what do organisms do? | They sit still and never change | *They eat or are eaten | They are always made of metal | They glow in the dark
exam: «A bacterium is a single-celled organism.» What is a single-celled organism? | *An organism made of just one cell | A plant with no leaves | A machine with many cells | An organism with a hundred cells
